.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn elf_link
performs direct merge/link of a set of input objects.
The plan API is a structured form that lets callers attach policy callbacks
for section merge behavior, archive extraction decisions, section GC roots,
incremental link notes, and symbol version handling.
.Pp
Plan map APIs expose a deterministic symbol mapping from merged output back to
input origin (input index/name, section, and value).
.Pp
.Fn elf_link_load_objects
and
.Fn elf_link_unload_objects
are utility helpers for bulk object lifecycle during linker front-end passes.
.Pp
.Fn elf_link_add_got_section ,
.Fn elf_link_add_plt_section ,
and
.Fn elf_link_add_dynamic_entry
provide builder helpers used when producing dynamic-link aware outputs.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn elf_link_plan_create
returns NULL on allocation failure.
.Pp
.Fn elf_link_resolve_symbol
returns NULL if the symbol cannot be resolved in inputs.
.Pp
.Fn elf_link_plan_map_entry
returns non-zero on success and 0 for out-of-range index.
.Pp
Other APIs return
.Dv ELF_OK
on success and an
.Vt elf_err_t
error code on failure.
